---
title: Quiet orchard crumble
servings: 6
oven:
  temperature: 180 C
  rack: middle
time:
  prep: 15 minutes
  bake: 40 minutes
tags: [pudding, autumn]
---

[- The fruit layer. Any firm orchard fruit will do;
   the fixture uses pears so the quantities stay simple. -]

Peel and chop @pears{5}(firm) and toss with @brown sugar{2%tbsp} and @cinnamon{1/2%tsp} in a #baking dish{}.

-- The topping is deliberately short on butter.
Rub @butter{75%g}(cold, cubed) into @plain flour{150%g} until it looks like damp sand, then stir in @rolled oats{50%g} and @demerara sugar{50%g}.

Scatter the topping over the fruit and bake for ~{40%minutes} until the edges bubble.
